IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa3-part9-rights.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 9 (Exercise of members' rights): ss 145 to 153;
-- lines 1879-2021 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. See coa3-part8-members.l4 for how to read JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING.
--
-- SEAMS taken as INPUTS: s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts (MAYBE BOOLEAN, the keel's); s 1173(1) UK regulated
-- market and EU regulated market (MAYBE BOOLEAN each); Schedule 5 Parts 3 and 4 (what the company may do to communicate
-- electronically; MAYBE BOOLEAN); the sections this Part points at (ss 291 to 293, 303, 310, 314, 319A, 324, 338, 338A, 342,
-- 360AA, 360BA, 423, 426, 431, 432, 527, 1145) are named in the enumerations below, not computed.

DECLARE `s 145 act under Part 9` IS ONE OF
    `s 149(2) the company accompanies the copy of the notice with the statement`
    `s 152(2) the member informs the company to what extent he is exercising the rights`
    `s 152(3) the member informs the company of the ways in which he is exercising the rights`
    `s 153(2) the company acts under the section`

-- ---- s 145: effect of provisions of articles as to enjoyment or exercise of members' rights ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:1881 | 145 Effect of provisions of articles as to enjoyment or exercise of members' rights
-- src:1882 | (1) This section applies where provision is made by a company's articles enabling a member to nominate another person or persons as entitled to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company.
@ref s 145(1) Where the articles enable a member to nominate another person (src:1881-1882)
GIVEN `the company's articles make provision enabling a member to nominate another person or persons as entitled to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company's articles make provision enabling a member to nominate another person or persons as entitled to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where provision is made by a company's articles enabling a member to nominate another person or persons as entitled to enjoy or exercise all or any specified rights of the member in relation to the company"

DECLARE `s 145(2) kind of act` IS ONE OF
    `s 145(2) an act required to be done by or in relation to the member`
    `s 145(2) an act that may be done by or in relation to the member`

-- src:1883 | (2) So far as is necessary to give effect to that provision, anything required or authorised by any provision of the Companies Acts to be done by or in relation to the member shall instead be done, or (as the case may be) may instead be done, by or in relation to the nominated person (or each of them) as if he were a member of the company.
@ref s 145(2) The act is done instead by or in relation to the nominated person (src:1883)
GIVEN `s 145(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 145(2) kind of act`
      `it is necessary to give effect to that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(2) the act is done, or may be done, by or in relation to the nominated person instead of the member` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 145(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (s 145(1))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of s 145(1) is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            IF `it is necessary to give effect to that provision`
            THEN CONSIDER kind
                 WHEN `s 145(2) an act required to be done by or in relation to the member` THEN JUST TRUE -- "shall instead be done"
                 WHEN `s 145(2) an act that may be done by or in relation to the member` THEN JUST TRUE -- "may instead be done"
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "So far as is necessary to give effect to that provision"
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision of the Companies Acts"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2(1) decides what is "the Companies Acts"

DECLARE `s 145(3) right` IS ONE OF
    `s 145(3)(a) the right to be sent a proposed written resolution (ss 291 and 293)`
    `s 145(3)(b) the right to require circulation of a written resolution (s 292)`
    `s 145(3)(c) the right to require directors to call a general meeting (s 303)`
    `s 145(3)(d) the right to notice of general meetings (s 310)`
    `s 145(3)(e) the right to require circulation of a statement (s 314)`
    `s 145(3)(ea) the right to ask a question at a meeting of a traded company (s 319A)`
    `s 145(3)(f) the right to appoint a proxy to act at a meeting (s 324)`
    `s 145(3)(g) the right to require circulation of a resolution for the AGM of a public company (s 338)`
    `s 145(3)(ga) the traded companies' members' power to include matters in the business dealt with at the AGM (s 338A)`
    `s 145(3)(gb) the confirmation of receipt of electronic voting of a traded company (s 360AA)`
    `s 145(3)(gc) the right of a traded company's member to confirmation of a vote after a general meeting (s 360BA)`
    `s 145(3)(h) the right to be sent a copy of the annual accounts and reports (s 423)`
    `s 145(3) another right`

-- src:1884 | (3) This applies, in particular, to the rights conferred by—
-- src:1885 | (a) sections 291 and 293 (right to be sent proposed written resolution);
-- src:1886 | (b) section 292 (right to require circulation of written resolution);
-- src:1887 | (c) section 303 (right to require directors to call general meeting);
-- src:1888 | (d) section 310 (right to notice of general meetings);
-- src:1889 | (e) section 314 (right to require circulation of a statement);
-- src:1890 | (ea) section 319A (right to ask question at meeting of traded company);
-- src:1891 | (f) section 324 (right to appoint proxy to act at meeting);
-- src:1892 | (g) section 338 (right to require circulation of resolution for AGM of public company); and
-- src:1893 | (ga) section 338A (traded companies: members' power to include matters in business dealt with at AGM);
-- src:1894 | (gb) 360AA (traded companies: confirmation of receipt of electronic voting);
-- src:1895 | (gc) 360BA (traded companies: right to confirmation of vote after a general meeting);
-- src:1896 | (h) section 423 (right to be sent a copy of annual accounts and reports).
@ref s 145(3) The rights to which s 145 applies in particular (src:1884-1896)
GIVEN right IS A `s 145(3) right`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(3) section 145 applies in particular to the right` MEANS
    CONSIDER right
    WHEN `s 145(3)(a) the right to be sent a proposed written resolution (ss 291 and 293)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(b) the right to require circulation of a written resolution (s 292)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(c) the right to require directors to call a general meeting (s 303)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(d) the right to notice of general meetings (s 310)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(e) the right to require circulation of a statement (s 314)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(ea) the right to ask a question at a meeting of a traded company (s 319A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(f) the right to appoint a proxy to act at a meeting (s 324)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(g) the right to require circulation of a resolution for the AGM of a public company (s 338)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(ga) the traded companies' members' power to include matters in the business dealt with at the AGM (s 338A)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(gb) the confirmation of receipt of electronic voting of a traded company (s 360AA)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(gc) the right of a traded company's member to confirmation of a vote after a general meeting (s 360BA)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3)(h) the right to be sent a copy of the annual accounts and reports (s 423)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 145(3) another right` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This applies, in particular, to the rights conferred by" (an "in particular" list)

-- src:1897 | (4) This section and any such provision as is mentioned in subsection (1)—
-- src:1898 | (a) do not confer rights enforceable against the company by anyone other than the member, and
-- src:1899 | (b) do not affect the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of the whole or part of a member's interest in the company.
@ref s 145(4)(a) A nomination confers no right enforceable against the company by anyone but the member (src:1897-1899)
GIVEN `the person seeking to enforce the right against the company is the nominated person and not the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4)(a) the person can enforce a right against the company by virtue of s 145 or the provision in the articles` MEANS
    IF `the person seeking to enforce the right against the company is the nominated person and not the member`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section and any such provision as is mentioned in subsection (1) (a) do not confer rights enforceable against the company by anyone other than the member"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by anyone other than the member" (the subsection says nothing of the member's own rights)

-- src:1897 | (4) This section and any such provision as is mentioned in subsection (1)—
-- src:1899 | (b) do not affect the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of the whole or part of a member's interest in the company.
@ref s 145(4)(b) A nomination does not affect the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition (src:1897 and src:1899)
GIVEN `the question concerns the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of the whole or part of a member's interest in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4)(b) s 145 or the provision in the articles affects the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of a member's interest` MEANS
    IF `the question concerns the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of the whole or part of a member's interest in the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not affect the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition of the whole or part of a member's interest in the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the requirements for an effective transfer or other disposition"

-- ---- s 146: traded companies: nomination of persons to enjoy information rights --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1901 | 146 Traded companies: nomination of persons to enjoy information rights
-- src:1902 | (1) This section applies to a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market.
@ref s 146(1) Companies to which the section applies (src:1901-1902)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1) this section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 1173(1) the shares are admitted to trading on an EU regulated market` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to a company whose shares are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market or an EU regulated market" (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1173(1) decides "UK regulated market" and "EU regulated market"

-- src:1903 | (2) A member of such a company who holds shares on behalf of another person may nominate that person to enjoy information rights.
@ref s 146(2) A member holding shares on behalf of another person may nominate that person (src:1903)
GIVEN `s 146(1) this section applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member holds shares on behalf of the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(2) the member may nominate the other person to enjoy information rights` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 146(1) this section applies to the company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person is a member of the company` AND `the member holds shares on behalf of the other person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of such a company who holds shares on behalf of another person"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such a company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 146(1) depends on s 1173(1)

DECLARE `s 146(3) right` IS ONE OF
    `s 146(3)(a) the right to receive a copy of all communications that the company sends to its members generally or to any class of its members that includes the person making the nomination`
    `s 146(3)(b)(i) the right conferred by section 431 or 432 (right to require copies of accounts and reports)`
    `s 146(3)(b)(ii) the right conferred by section 1145 (right to require hard copy version of document or information provided in another form)`
    `s 146(3) another right`

-- src:1904 | (3) “Information rights” means—
-- src:1905 | (a) the right to receive a copy of all communications that the company sends to its members generally or to any class of its members that includes the person making the nomination, and
-- src:1906 | (b) the rights conferred by—
-- src:1907 | (i) section 431 or 432 (right to require copies of accounts and reports), and
-- src:1908 | (ii) section 1145 (right to require hard copy version of document or information provided in another form).
@ref s 146(3) "Information rights" (src:1904-1908)
GIVEN right IS A `s 146(3) right`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(3) the right is one of the "information rights"` MEANS
    CONSIDER right
    WHEN `s 146(3)(a) the right to receive a copy of all communications that the company sends to its members generally or to any class of its members that includes the person making the nomination` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 146(3)(b)(i) the right conferred by section 431 or 432 (right to require copies of accounts and reports)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 146(3)(b)(ii) the right conferred by section 1145 (right to require hard copy version of document or information provided in another form)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 146(3) another right` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Information rights” means— (a) the right to receive a copy of all communications ... and (b) the rights conferred by (i) section 431 or 432 ..., and (ii) section 1145"

@ref s 146(3)(a) The communications a copy of which the person has the right to receive (src:1905)
GIVEN `the company sends the communication to its members generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company sends the communication to a class of its members that includes the person making the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(3)(a) the person has the right to receive a copy of the communication` MEANS
    IF `the company sends the communication to its members generally` OR `the company sends the communication to a class of its members that includes the person making the nomination`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all communications that the company sends to its members generally or to any class of its members that includes the person making the nomination"

-- src:1909 | (4) The reference in subsection (3)(a) to communications that a company sends to its members generally includes the company's annual accounts and reports.
@ref s 146(4) Annual accounts and reports are communications sent to members generally (src:1909)
GIVEN `the document is the company's annual accounts and reports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(4) the document is within the communications that the company sends to its members generally` MEANS
    IF `the document is the company's annual accounts and reports`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "communications that a company sends to its members generally includes the company's annual accounts and reports" (an inclusive definition says nothing of other documents)

-- The second sentence of s 146(4) ("For the application of section 426 ... see subsection (5) of that section") is a signpost: coverage row `inert`, reason 1.

-- src:1911 | (5) A company need not act on a nomination purporting to relate to certain information rights only.
@ref s 146(5) A nomination relating to certain information rights only (src:1911)
GIVEN `the nomination purports to relate to certain information rights only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(5) the company need not act on the nomination` MEANS
    IF `the nomination purports to relate to certain information rights only`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company need not act on a nomination purporting to relate to certain information rights only"

-- ---- s 147: information rights: form in which copies are to be provided --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1912 | 147 Information rights: form in which copies to be provided
-- src:1913 | (1) This section applies as regards the form in which copies are to be provided to a person nominated under section 146 (nomination of person to enjoy information rights).
@ref s 147(1) The form in which copies are provided (src:1912-1913)
GIVEN `the copies are to be provided to a person nominated under section 146` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the copies are to be provided to a person nominated under section 146`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the form in which copies are to be provided to a person nominated under section 146"

-- src:1914 | (2) If the person to be nominated wishes to receive hard copy communications, he must—
-- src:1915 | (a) request the person making the nomination to notify the company of that fact, and
-- src:1916 | (b) provide an address to which such copies may be sent.
@ref s 147(2) A person who wishes to receive hard copy communications (src:1914-1916)
GIVEN `the person to be nominated wishes to receive hard copy communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(2) the person to be nominated must request the person making the nomination to notify the company of that fact and provide an address` MEANS
    IF `the person to be nominated wishes to receive hard copy communications`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the person to be nominated wishes to receive hard copy communications, he must"

-- "This must be done before the nomination is made": the day it was done must be an earlier day (fork F18).
-- src:1917 | This must be done before the nomination is made.
@ref s 147(2) This must be done before the nomination is made (src:1917)
GIVEN `the date on which the request was made and the address provided` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the nomination is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(2) the request was made and the address provided before the nomination was made` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the request was made and the address provided` LESS THAN `the date on which the nomination is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This must be done before the nomination is made"

-- src:1918 | (3) If having received such a request the person making the nomination—
-- src:1919 | (a) notifies the company that the nominated person wishes to receive hard copy communications, and
-- src:1920 | (b) provides the company with that address,
-- src:1921 | the right of the nominated person is to receive hard copy communications accordingly.
@ref s 147(3) The right to hard copy communications (src:1918-1921)
GIVEN `the person making the nomination has received such a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the nomination notifies the company that the nominated person wishes to receive hard copy communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the nomination provides the company with that address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(3) the right of the nominated person is to receive hard copy communications` MEANS
    IF `the person making the nomination has received such a request` AND `the person making the nomination notifies the company that the nominated person wishes to receive hard copy communications` AND `the person making the nomination provides the company with that address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If having received such a request the person making the nomination (a) notifies the company ..., and (b) provides the company with that address, the right of the nominated person is to receive hard copy communications accordingly"

-- src:1922 | (4) This is subject to the provisions of Parts 3 and 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by company) under which the company may take steps to enable it to communicate in electronic form or by means of a website.
@ref s 147(4) Subject to Parts 3 and 4 of Schedule 5 (src:1922)
GIVEN `sch 5 Parts 3 and 4 the company has taken steps to enable it to communicate in electronic form or by means of a website` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(4) the right under s 147(3) is unaffected by Parts 3 and 4 of Schedule 5` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 5 Parts 3 and 4 the company has taken steps to enable it to communicate in electronic form or by means of a website`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the provisions of Schedule 5 under which "the company may take steps" are not engaged when it has taken none
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This is subject to the provisions of Parts 3 and 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by company)"; Schedule 5 is not among my sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 5 Parts 3 and 4

-- src:1923 | (5) If no such notification is given (or no address is provided), the nominated person is taken to have agreed that documents or information may be sent or supplied to him by the company by means of a website.
@ref s 147(5) No notification or no address: agreement to a website (src:1923)
GIVEN `no such notification is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no address is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(5) the nominated person is taken to have agreed that documents or information may be sent or supplied to him by means of a website` MEANS
    IF `no such notification is given` OR `no address is provided`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such notification is given (or no address is provided)"

-- src:1924 | (6) That agreement—
-- src:1925 | (a) may be revoked by the nominated person, and
@ref s 147(6)(a) The agreement may be revoked (src:1924-1925)
GIVEN `the nominated person is taken to have agreed under s 147(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(6)(a) the agreement may be revoked by the nominated person` MEANS
    IF `the nominated person is taken to have agreed under s 147(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "That agreement"

-- src:1924 | (6) That agreement—
-- src:1926 | (b) does not affect his right under section 1145 to require a hard copy version of a document or information provided in any other form.
@ref s 147(6)(b) The agreement does not affect the right under s 1145 (src:1924 and src:1926)
GIVEN `the nominated person is taken to have agreed under s 147(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(6)(b) the agreement affects the right under s 1145 to require a hard copy version of a document or information provided in any other form` MEANS
    IF `the nominated person is taken to have agreed under s 147(5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That agreement ... does not affect his right under section 1145 to require a hard copy version of a document or information provided in any other form"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "That agreement"

-- ---- s 148: termination or suspension of nomination ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1927 | 148 Termination or suspension of nomination
-- src:1928 | (1) The following provisions have effect in relation to a nomination under section 146 (nomination of person to enjoy information rights).
@ref s 148(1) The provisions have effect in relation to a nomination under s 146 (src:1927-1928)
GIVEN `the nomination is a nomination under section 146` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(1) the provisions of s 148 have effect in relation to the nomination` MEANS
    IF `the nomination is a nomination under section 146`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a nomination under section 146"

DECLARE `s 148(2) person making the request` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(2) the member`
    `s 148(2) the nominated person`
    `s 148(2) someone else`

-- src:1929 | (2) The nomination may be terminated at the request of the member or of the nominated person.
@ref s 148(2) Termination at the request of the member or of the nominated person (src:1929)
GIVEN requester IS A `s 148(2) person making the request`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(2) the nomination may be terminated at the request` MEANS
    CONSIDER requester
    WHEN `s 148(2) the member` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(2) the nominated person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(2) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the request of the member or of the nominated person"

DECLARE `s 148(3) event in relation to the member or the nominated person` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(3)(a) the death of an individual`
    `s 148(3)(a) the bankruptcy of an individual`
    `s 148(3)(b) the dissolution of a body corporate`
    `s 148(3)(b) the making of an order for the winding up of a body corporate` HAS
        `s 148(3)(b) the order is made for the purposes of reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 148(3) another event`

-- src:1930 | (3) The nomination ceases to have effect on the occurrence in relation to the member or the nominated person of any of the following—
-- src:1931 | (a) in the case of an individual, death or bankruptcy;
-- src:1932 | (b) in the case of a body corporate, dissolution or the making of an order for the winding up of the body otherwise than for the purposes of reconstruction.
@ref s 148(3) The nomination ceases to have effect (src:1930-1932)
GIVEN event IS A `s 148(3) event in relation to the member or the nominated person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(3) the nomination ceases to have effect on the event` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `s 148(3)(a) the death of an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(3)(a) the bankruptcy of an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(3)(b) the dissolution of a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(3)(b) the making of an order for the winding up of a body corporate` reconstruction THEN
        IF reconstruction
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the making of an order for the winding up of the body otherwise than for the purposes of reconstruction" (fork F15)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(3) another event` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following" lists four events without "only"

DECLARE `s 148(4)(a) proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(4)(a)(i) the sequestration of a person's estate`
    `s 148(4)(a)(ii) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016)`
    `s 148(4)(a) another proceeding`

-- src:1933 | (4) In subsection (3)—
-- src:1934 | (a) the reference to bankruptcy includes—
-- src:1935 | (i) the sequestration of a person's estate, and
-- src:1936 | (ii) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016); and
@ref s 148(4)(a) The reference to bankruptcy includes (src:1933-1936)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `s 148(4)(a) proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(4)(a) the proceeding is bankruptcy for the purposes of s 148(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `s 148(4)(a)(i) the sequestration of a person's estate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(4)(a)(ii) a person's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(4)(a) another proceeding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to bankruptcy includes" (an inclusive definition says nothing of other proceedings)

DECLARE `s 148(4)(b) order or proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 148(4)(b)(i) an order for winding up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    `s 148(4)(b)(ii) a corresponding proceeding under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
    `s 148(4)(b) another order or proceeding`

-- src:1933 | (4) In subsection (3)—
-- src:1937 | (b) the reference to the making of an order for winding up is to—
-- src:1938 | (i) the making of such an order under the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), or
-- src:1939 | (ii) any corresponding proceeding under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 148(4)(b) The reference to the making of an order for winding up is to (src:1933 and src:1937-1939)
