`s 148(4)(b) the order or proceeding is the making of an order for winding up for the purposes of s 148(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `s 148(4)(b)(i) an order for winding up under the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(4)(b)(ii) a corresponding proceeding under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 148(4)(b) another order or proceeding` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the reference to the making of an order for winding up is to— (i) ... or (ii) ..." (read as a definition by "is to", against the open "includes" of paragraph (a); fork F17)

-- src:1940 | (5) The effect of any nominations made by a member is suspended at any time when there are more nominated persons than the member has shares in the company.
@ref s 148(5) Suspension where there are more nominated persons than shares (src:1940)
GIVEN `the number of nominated persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares the member has in the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 148(5) the effect of the nominations made by the member is suspended` MEANS
    IF `the number of nominated persons` GREATER THAN `the number of shares the member has in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time when there are more nominated persons than the member has shares in the company"

-- src:1941 | (6) Where—
