    IF `the nomination has been terminated or suspended`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The termination or suspension of a nomination means that the company is not required to act on it"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The termination or suspension of a nomination"

-- src:1950 | (8) The termination or suspension of a nomination means that the company is not required to act on it.
-- src:1951 | It does not prevent the company from continuing to do so, to such extent or for such period as it thinks fit.
