GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company sends a copy of a notice of a meeting to a person nominated under section 146`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company sends a copy of a notice of a meeting to a person nominated under section 146"

-- src:1954 | (2) The copy of the notice must be accompanied by a statement that—
-- src:1955 | (a) he may have a right under an agreement between him and the member by whom he was nominated to be appointed, or to have someone else appointed, as a proxy for the meeting, and
-- src:1956 | (b) if he has no such right or does not wish to exercise it, he may have a right under such an agreement to give instructions to the member as to the exercise of voting rights.
@ref s 149(2) The copy of the notice must be accompanied by a statement (src:1954-1956)
GIVEN `s 149(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2) the copy of the notice must be accompanied by the statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 149(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (s 149(1))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of s 149(1) is not known

@ref s 149(2) The copy of the notice must be accompanied by a statement (src:1954-1956)
GIVEN `the statement says that he may have a right under an agreement between him and the member to be appointed, or to have someone else appointed, as a proxy for the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that, if he has no such right or does not wish to exercise it, he may have a right under such an agreement to give instructions to the member as to the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2) the statement contains what s 149(2) requires` MEANS
    IF       `the statement says that he may have a right under an agreement between him and the member to be appointed, or to have someone else appointed, as a proxy for the meeting`
         AND `the statement says that, if he has no such right or does not wish to exercise it, he may have a right under such an agreement to give instructions to the member as to the exercise of voting rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy of the notice must be accompanied by a statement that (a) he may have a right under an agreement ... to be appointed, or to have someone else appointed, as a proxy for the meeting, and (b) if he has no such right or does not wish to exercise it, he may have a right under such an agreement to give instructions to the member as to the exercise of voting rights" (a bare "must"; fork F8)

@ref s 149(2) The copy of the notice must be accompanied by a statement (src:1954-1956)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 145 act under Part 9`
`s 149(2) the company must accompany the copy of the notice with the statement (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 149(2) the company accompanies the copy of the notice with the statement`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the copy of the notice was not accompanied by the statement that s 149(2) requires"

