    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 149(3) speaks of the copy to which s 149 applies
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer of s 149(1) is not known

