-- ---- s 152: exercise of rights where shares are held on behalf of others ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1984 | 152 Exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others: exercise in different ways
-- src:1985 | (1) Where a member holds shares in a company on behalf of more than one person—
-- src:1986 | (a) rights attached to the shares, and
-- src:1987 | (b) rights under any enactment exercisable by virtue of holding the shares,
-- src:1988 | need not all be exercised, and if exercised, need not all be exercised in the same way.
@ref s 152(1) Rights need not all be exercised, or all in the same way (src:1984-1988)
GIVEN `the member holds shares in the company on behalf of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(1) the member may exercise some only of the rights, or exercise them in different ways` MEANS
    IF `the member holds shares in the company on behalf of more than one person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a member holds shares in a company on behalf of more than one person (a) rights attached to the shares, and (b) rights under any enactment exercisable by virtue of holding the shares, need not all be exercised, and if exercised, need not all be exercised in the same way"

-- src:1989 | (2) A member who exercises such rights but does not exercise all his rights, must inform the company to what extent he is exercising the rights.
@ref s 152(2) A member who does not exercise all his rights must inform the company (src:1989)
GIVEN `the member holds shares in the company on behalf of more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member exercises such rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member does not exercise all his rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 152(2) the member must inform the company to what extent he is exercising the rights` MEANS
    IF NOT `the member holds shares in the company on behalf of more than one person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such rights" (the rights of s 152(1)(a) and (b))
    ELSE IF `the member exercises such rights` AND `the member does not exercise all his rights`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member who exercises such rights but does not exercise all his rights"

@ref s 152(2) A member who does not exercise all his rights must inform the company (src:1989)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 145 act under Part 9`
`s 152(2) the member must inform the company to what extent he is exercising the rights (duty)` MEANS
    PARTY Member
    MUST `s 152(2) the member informs the company to what extent he is exercising the rights`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Member BECAUSE "the member did not inform the company to what extent he is exercising the rights"

